<MECA ID = "T010005A909C067" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "10Oct2005"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Engine Features (High Performance / Low Fuel Consumption)</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>By adopting Dual VVT-i, optimal valve timing is set according to engine conditions in various speed ranges, achieving higher output, higher torque and lower emissions.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Roller rocker arms have been adopted in the DOHC4-valve cylinder head, and the valve included angle has been narrowed to 25.6 degrees, giving the combustion chamber a compact shape with an excellent S/V<HINTREF     REFID = "H478010005A909C06701"/> ratio. In addition, the adoption of fine-tip long-reach iridium spark plugs allows optimal placement of the cylinder head water jacket, raising the knock limit.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>High-flow intake ports and slanted squish combustion chambers are adopted, improving performance by increasing intake air volume.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A thin-wall cast aluminum intake manifold is adopted, and port diameter, port length and port shape are optimized, achieving higher torque and lower fuel consumption across the entire operating range. In addition, engine performance has been improved by minimizing intake pressure loss.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Optimized exhaust ports and the adoption of a stainless steel pipe exhaust manifold improve low to mid speed torque.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A one-way clutch is provided in the alternator pulley, allowing lower accessory belt tension and reducing friction to improve fuel economy.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A roller rocker type valve mechanism is adopted, together with a new type of resin coating on the pistons, low-tension piston rings, and uniform bore wall temperature through improved cylinder bore roundness, greatly reducing friction in the valve train and reciprocating/rotating parts.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>ACIS (Acoustic Control Induction System: variable intake system) has been adopted. The intake pipe length and surge tank capacity are varied to increase torque across the entire range.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<HINT>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT ID = "H478010005A909C06701">S/V: Surface area/volume of the combustion chamber. The lower the S/V ratio, the lower the cooling loss and the more effectively fuel can be used.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></HINT></MECA>

<MECA ID = "T010005A909C068" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "10Oct2005"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Engine Features (Low Emissions)</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>A stainless steel exhaust manifold with an integrated three-way catalytic converter has been adopted. Placing the catalyst directly below the engine improves catalyst warm-up, improving emission performance immediately after engine start. In addition, adopting an A/F sensor enables precise air-fuel ratio control, complying with the "Arial 17 Emission Regulations" and achieving the "Arial 17 Standard Emissions 75% Reduction Level (SU-LEV)".</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></MECA>

<MECA ID = "T010005A909C069" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "10Oct2005"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Engine Features (Lightweight / Compact)</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>The cylinder block is made of aluminum alloy to reduce weight.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>By adopting a serpentine drive in which the accessories are driven by 1 belt, the overall length of the engine has been shortened.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>The intake manifold is made of thin-wall cast aluminum to reduce weight.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>The exhaust manifold is made of stainless steel, and the cylinder head mounting flange is a thin-wall pressed part to reduce weight.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>The charcoal canister is integrated with the fuel pump, reducing the number of parts and saving space.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A resin surge tank and resin fuel delivery pipe are adopted to reduce weight.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A full-fabric air element that does not use an outer frame or rubber seal is adopted, making the air cleaner case smaller.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></MECA>

<MECA ID = "T010005A909C070" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "10Oct2005"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Engine Features (Low Vibration, Low Noise, Quietness)</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>A high-rigidity aluminum alloy oil pan with an integrated stiffener is adopted, improving the coupling rigidity with the power plant and reducing vibration and noise.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A high-strength, high-rigidity forged steel crankshaft with 4 journals and 5 balance weights is adopted, reducing weight while reducing vibration and noise through optimal placement of the balance weights.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A 2-system intake system has been adopted. The 2-system intake valve is switched in 2 stages according to driving conditions to reduce intake noise.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>An electric cooling fan system is adopted, controlling the fan speed according to operating conditions to ensure quietness.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></MECA>

<MECA ID = "T010005A909Aa04" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "10Oct2005"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Engine Features (Reliability)</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>An MRE (Magneto Resistance Element) type camshaft position sensor has been adopted. The crank position at startup can be detected early, improving engine startability.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Cranking hold control has been adopted. Cranking continues until complete engine start is detected, ensuring reliable engine starting.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Using the "TaSCAN" diagnostic tool, accurate and detailed diagnosis is possible, such as reading SAE-standard diagnostic trouble codes and data and performing Active Tests.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></MECA>

<MECA ID = "T010005A909C071" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "10Oct2005"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Engine Features (Serviceability)</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>The adoption of fine-tip long-reach iridium spark plugs extends the maintenance interval.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>An element-replacement type oil filter is adopted out of consideration for the environment.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Hydraulic lash adjusters are adopted, eliminating the need for valve clearance adjustment.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Quick connectors are adopted at each fuel pipe joint, improving serviceability.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></MECA>
</PARA>
